# Roblox Open Cloud — credentials for the tools in tools/*.
#
# HOW TO USE: copy this file to `.env` and paste the real values there. `.env` is gitignored and must stay
# that way: an Open Cloud key with DataStore scope can erase every player's save, and one with asset scope can
# publish to your account. Never paste a key into a chat, a commit, an issue or a log — if one is ever exposed,
# revoke it at https://create.roblox.com/dashboard/credentials and issue a new one.
#
# LEAST PRIVILEGE: grant only the scopes for what you actually want automated, and restrict the key by IP and
# expiry date on the same page. Adding a scope later takes ten seconds; un-leaking a key takes the rest of the
# project's life.

# The API key itself (Creator Hub → Credentials → API Keys).
ROBLOX_API_KEY=

# A SEPARATE key for `npm run cloud -- erase` (right to erasure), with ONLY the data store permissions it needs:
# read, list, update and delete entries, for this universe, restricted to your IP. The key that can delete saves
# should not also publish the game, and the one that publishes should not delete saves. Without it, erase falls
# back to ROBLOX_API_KEY and says so. See docs/CREATOR_HUB.md (Data Stores manager, RTBF).
ROBLOX_ERASE_API_KEY=

# Which experience and place the tools act on (Creator Hub → your experience → the URL carries both ids).
ROBLOX_UNIVERSE_ID=
ROBLOX_PLACE_ID=

# Who owns what `npm run cloud -- upload-art` uploads (the town's textures): your user id, or the group's id if the
# experience belongs to a group (then leave the user id empty). The key needs the Assets API scopes (asset:read and
# asset:write) for that creator.
# CI: the GitHub Actions job `assets` uploads on every push to main with repository SECRETS of these same names
# (ROBLOX_API_KEY -- there a separate key, Assets only -- and ROBLOX_CREATOR_USER_ID); docs/CREATOR_HUB.md,
# "Open Cloud na CI". Nothing in this file is ever read by the CI.
ROBLOX_CREATOR_USER_ID=
ROBLOX_CREATOR_GROUP_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scopes, and what each one buys us. Grant the ones you want, leave the rest off.
#
#   universe-places:write   Publish the place built by `rojo build` straight from here or from CI, so a
#                           release stops depending on somebody having Studio open.
#   asset:read + asset:write    Upload images and audio (the UI skin was 14 textures uploaded by hand; the town's
#                           art goes up with `npm run cloud -- upload-art`).
#   universe-datastores:read    Read a player's save to debug it. Read-only is enough for that.
#   universe-datastores:write   Repair a broken save. Powerful and rarely needed: leave it OFF until the day
#                           there is a save to repair, then turn it off again.
#   universe.place.luau-execution-session:write   Run Luau against the published place without Studio.
#
# WHAT IT CANNOT DO, so we do not plan around it: it does not change experience settings (ChatVersion, API
# services, permissions — those stay in Studio and the Creator Hub), and it does not replace a playtest.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MEASURED on the key in use (npm run cloud -- whoami), 2026-09-23:
#
#   universe (read)        permitted
#   place (read)           permitted
#   data-stores (read)     permitted -- this is what lets `npm run cloud -- save <userId>` inspect a live
#                          save without Studio, which used to need a playtest and a print of the output
#   user-restrictions      permitted (the ban list)
#   assets                 NOT on this key
#
# Write scopes are deliberately NOT probed: a probe of a write IS a write. We find out the first time one is
# used for real, which is why `npm run cloud -- publish` explains what it is about to do before doing it.
